# Project rules

## Plan-first workflow

1. Read `PLAN.md` and `docs/PHASES.md` before starting work.
2. Work one phase at a time; stop at phase gates for verification.
3. Do not begin the next phase until the gate is approved.

## Engineering standards

- TypeScript strict mode; small, focused diffs.
- Never commit `.env` or API keys.
- Run tests before reporting a phase gate.
- Match existing naming and module boundaries.

## Invariants (non-negotiable)

See `docs/INVARIANTS.md`. Key points:

- Zod schema is the single source of truth for extracted data shape.
- `franc` is metadata-only — never translates or modifies LLM input.
- All LLM calls go through `src/services/invoice-extractor.ts`.
- Pipeline depends on `src/ports/` interfaces, not concrete services.
- Domain layer has no LangChain imports.

## Commits

Follow `docs/COMMITS.md`: Conventional Commits + co-author trailer.
